# public/_headers — response headers for the Cloudflare Workers Static Assets deployment.
# `expo export --platform web` copies public/ into dist/, so this file ships with every build.
# Rules accumulate top-down; `! Name` removes a header set by a more general rule above.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is REPORT-ONLY for the first certification cycle: it must produce
# browser console reports (evidence), not break the admin web. Promote to enforcing only after the
# routing/auth certification runs clean. Known Expo facts behind the directives:
#   - every generated document carries exactly one inline script, the constant
#     `globalThis.__EXPO_ROUTER_HYDRATE__=true;` → allowed by its SHA-256 (identical across
#     exports and Expo SDK 56; re-derive after an Expo upgrade: sha256 of the script body, base64);
#   - react-native-web pre-renders inline `style=""` attributes and a <style> tag → 'unsafe-inline'
#     for styles is required by the framework output;
#   - the only backend origin is the Production Supabase project host (a public identifier);
#   - no WebSocket (Realtime) is used by the admin web; no Sentry DSN is configured.
#
# Caching: one conservative revalidation policy for EVERY response. `not_found_handling:
# "single-page-application"` (wrangler.jsonc) answers unmatched paths — including a missing
# /_expo/static/... or /assets/... file — with the HTML shell, and `_headers` matches by URL only,
# so a long-lived/immutable rule on those prefixes would let a browser pin that fallback document
# to a hashed asset URL (a rollback hazard). Long-lived caching for hashed assets may be
# reconsidered only after missing asset paths return genuine 404 responses. Content-hashed bundle
# names plus ETag revalidation keep every deployment safe under this policy.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-67fhrP0+BkBqmgGGXTtgiVO/9EQs3QruYNU/7fnRkI8='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://lkigkltvstlxfdztffds.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Keep the workers.dev certification hostname out of search indexes. A future custom domain does
# not match this rule and stays indexable.
https://quickserve.:subdomain.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
